t 6, 1945, Tsutomu Yamaguchi was in Hiroshima on a business trip when the first bomb detonated less than two miles away.", "s": 7.155, "e": 18.343}, {"text": "Badly burned with ruptured eardrums, he spent the night in an air-raid shelter and caught a train back to his hometown: Nagasaki.", "s": 18.463, "e": 27.548}, {"text": "Three days later, while he was describing the blast to his boss, the second atomic bomb dropped outside his office window.", "s": 27.668, "e": 35.991}, {"text": "He survived again and lived to age 93.", "s": 36.111, "e": 39.524}]}